###############################################################################
# Simple Graphs - ENGINE: the plot's line style.
#
# ENGINE FILE. Subject to the two rules in README_GENERICITY_INVESTIGATION.md:
#   1. no sg_engine_* file names a game object type;
#   2. no sg_engine_* file references anything sg_c_*.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THIS FILE HOLDS THE STYLE AND NOT THE DECODE EXPRESSIONS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Part 3 of the investigation proposed this file as "line template + decode
# expressions". Only the first half moved, deliberately.
#
# The decode expressions cannot move as they stand. They live inside `from` and
# `to` on a `line`, and the widget around them carries the `datamodel` and the
# `visible` that name a specific object type. Lifting them out means declaring
# a `type` here with a `block` for the datamodel, and having the consumer
# supply it via `blockoverride`. That is the "one template instantiated N
# times" mitigation the investigation flagged as the realistic ceiling - and
# explicitly did NOT attempt or verify.
#
# This repo has never declared its own `type` with its own `block`. A bad one
# fails the way everything in CK3 GUI fails: silently, with an empty
# gui_warnings.log and a plot that simply does not draw. Betting the one
# feature that works on an unverified mechanism, during a change that is
# otherwise a rename, is the trade this file declines to make. The expressions
# stay inline in the consumer window, with the packing contract documented in
# sg_engine_storage.txt, which is where the encoding they undo is defined.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY A SEPARATE FILE IS SAFE, VERIFIED RATHER THAN ASSUMED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The consumer window references sg_engine_line_data from a DIFFERENT file that
# sorts alphabetically BEFORE this one (sg_c_... before sg_engine_...), so this
# only works if CK3 resolves templates after parsing every .gui rather than in
# load order. It does. In the 1.19.0.6 install there are 27 same-directory
# cases in game/gui where the using file sorts before the defining file, e.g.
#   map_icon_layer.gui       uses combat_prediction_tooltip
#     defined in             map_icon_layer_templates.gui
#   chariot_race_widget_types.gui  uses PivotalMomentTransitionAnimation
#     defined in                    tournament_widget_types.gui
#   animation.gui            uses Mask_Rough_Edges
#     defined in             backgrounds.gui
# plus 3,212 cross-file template uses overall. Load order does not constrain
# template resolution.
#
# The name was checked for collisions against game/gui, jomini/gui and
# clausewitz/gui: zero hits. GUI is first-in-only-served, so a collision would
# mean this file is silently ignored with no error.
#
# The vanilla templates this one follows (Line_Domicile_*, which render inside
# a scrollbox at window_domicile.gui:3508) do NOT set effectname, i.e. they use
# the default line effect rather than PdxGuiLineScreenSpace. This one matches.
###############################################################################

template sg_engine_line_data
{
	width = 3
	line_cap = yes
	color = { 1.0 1.0 1.0 1.0 }
	texture = "gfx/lines/white.dds"
	uv_scale = { 1.0 1.0 }
	mask = "gfx/lines/white.dds"
	mask_uv_scale = { 1.0 1.0 }
}
